{"name":"Burnt Crimson","hex":"#582124","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burnt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of burn"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Damaged or injured by fire or heat.","Carbonised."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burnt"},{"term":"crimson","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep, slightly bluish red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a deep red colour.","Immodest. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crimson"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crimson","blocks":[{"text":"Crimson is a rich, deep red color, inclining to purple. It originally meant the color of the kermes dye produced from a scale insect, Kermes vermilio, but the name is now sometimes also used as a generic term for slightly bluish-red colors that are between red and rose. It is the national color of Nepal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg/330px-Maple_Leaf_Red_Ground_2000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crimson","wikidata":"Q303826"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg/500px-Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg/500px-Oaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOaxaca_de_Ju%C3%A1rez%2C_detalles_07.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG/500px-California_Palace_of_the_Legion_of_Honor_120_2015-01-03.JPG?ut